    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "true, but if you look at the actual gap in IQ scores between different groups, isn't it harder to explain away that just with \"environment\"? the people i'm reading seem to say the math itself shows a biological component that environment can't fully account for. can you explain why they believe the data points to something more permanent rather than just social factors?",
